%% The ops copilot as built (Phases 07-08). Source: packages/ai-harness and
%% apps/api/src/modules/copilot; decisions in docs/adr/0020-0024.
%% The runtime is our own OpenAI-compatible tool loop rather than an SDK's agent loop:
%% it calls the handlers itself, so tool_start / tool_end are facts it observes and
%% times, not events it hopes the SDK emits (ADR 0021). Still outstanding: the Bedrock
%% smoke run, for lack of AWS credentials (ADR 0003).
sequenceDiagram
    participant Ops as Ops user
    participant Web as React SPA
    participant API as CopilotController<br/>@Roles('ops','ops_admin')
    participant Session as CopilotSessionUseCases<br/>+ ChatTurnService (harness)
    participant Runtime as OpenAiToolLoopRuntime<br/>(behind AgentRuntime)
    participant Tools as Tools built for this request<br/>(caller resolved inside each handler)
    participant Service as Application services<br/>(OrderService, InventoryService, ...)
    participant LLM as LiteLLM alias default-chat<br/>→ Claude Haiku 4.5 on Bedrock

    Ops->>Web: "which orders are about to expire?"
    Web->>API: POST /copilot/sessions/:id/messages (SSE via fetch, token in header, never in the URL)
    API->>Session: execute(actor, sessionId, message)
    Session->>Session: load ai.chat_sessions by (tenant_id, owner_user_id, id)<br/>another tenant's session → 404
    Session->>Tools: build tools from the caller's Actor<br/>get_inventory_status, find_orders, explain_order_blockers,<br/>list_expiring_reservations, get_contract_price,<br/>inventory_movement_history, propose_stock_adjustment
    Note over Tools: Tool schemas have no tenant field for the model to fill.<br/>get_contract_price takes a customer org code and checks it<br/>with assertOrgInScope before pricing.
    Session->>Runtime: stream(input with tools)

    Runtime->>LLM: chat completion with tool definitions
    LLM-->>Runtime: text and/or a tool call

    alt model calls a tool
        Runtime-->>Web: RunEvent tool_start { callId, name, input }
        Runtime->>Tools: handler(input), validated by the tool's zod schema
        Tools->>Service: service call with the same Actor and OrgScope<br/>(assertRole and scoped SQL inside the service)
        Service-->>Tools: result
        Tools-->>Runtime: result
        Runtime-->>Web: RunEvent tool_end { callId, name, ok, durationMs }
        Runtime->>LLM: continue with the tool result<br/>(capped by COPILOT_MAX_TOOL_CALLS_PER_TURN)
    end

    Runtime-->>Web: text deltas
    Runtime-->>Session: final result
    Session->>Session: persist the transcript to the owned session

    Note over Tools,Service: The only write tool, propose_stock_adjustment, creates a proposal.<br/>A person approves it (no self-approval, enforced by a CHECK), and approval<br/>runs the existing AdjustStockUseCase.
